{
  "overflowPolicy": {
    "_comment": "Ordering of overflow images (no qualifying phenotype). Filename-hinted images anchor at their hinted slot index; unhinted images anchor at unhintedAnchor - between the main-view slots (front/back/side, det0-2) and the detail/label/material slots (det3+), so a detail-hinted file can never jump ahead of the family's main shots. onModelFirst ranks hero-is-human=TRUE images before packshots within the same anchor.",
    "unhintedAnchor": 2.5,
    "onModelFirst": true
  },
  "_comment_ghost": "T-5040 (2026-08-04): ghost-front/back/side were deleted from the taxonomy and removed from every slot below. Their rules had become character-identical to front/back/side-packshot once clipping-path went (T-5030), so they could never be assigned and the entries here were dead weight. Every slot that listed a ghost phenotype also listed its packshot equivalent, so no slot lost its filler and no image changes slot. *-packshot now covers both the flat-lay and the ghost-mannequin case - see imagePhenotypes.md.",
  "_comment_pack": "default.det6 ('pack') deliberately carries an empty phenotypes list: its packaging-visible feature was removed in T-4700. It is NOT dead - ImageOrderer.ResolveHintSlot still uses the keyword as an overflow anchor, so a *_packaging.jpg still sorts to this position. Do not delete the slot; do not invent a phenotype for it.",
